# Copy this file to oauth_bff.env and fill in real values.
# oauth_bff.env is gitignored so prod values are never committed.
#
# Single source for the OAuth + App Links + BFF flow, consumed by both:
#   1. Flutter (via flutter build --dart-define-from-file=android/oauth_bff.env)
#   2. android/app/build.gradle.kts (reads OAUTH_BFF_HOST and feeds it to
#      AndroidManifest's App Links intent-filter via the ${bffHost}
#      manifest placeholder)
#
# If oauth_bff.env is absent, the build still succeeds: empty values flow
# through and OAuthBffConfig.isFullyConfigured returns false (UI hides the
# login entry point), and the Android intent-filter falls back to a
# non-resolvable .invalid host so it cannot bind to a stale value.
#
# Format constraints (so both Flutter's .env loader and Java
# Properties().load() agree on the result):
#   - One KEY=VALUE per line.
#   - Comments start with '#' at the beginning of a line. Inline '#' inside
#     a value is treated as part of the value.
#   - Values must NOT contain '=' (the first '=' is the key/value
#     separator). URL query strings would break this rule — keep
#     OAUTH_AUTHORIZE_ENDPOINT to the path-only form, no query.
#   - Values must NOT contain a backslash; Java Properties interprets it as
#     an escape while Flutter's loader does not.
#   - No quoting; values are taken verbatim, including trailing spaces.
NICONICO_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
OAUTH_BFF_HOST=your-bff.example.com
OAUTH_AUTHORIZE_ENDPOINT=https://your-idp.example.com/authorize
